    <desc>Close, restart or keep the terminal when its shell or command exits.</desc>
  </info>

  <title>Set behavior on command exit</title>

<p>You can set the terminal to close, restart or remain open when the shell
  or a custom command exits:</p>
  <steps>
<item><p>Press the menu button in the top-right corner of the window and select <gui style="menuitem">Preferences</gui>.</p></item><item><p>In the <gui>Profiles</gui> group, click the profile you want to change. Its settings open on a page of their own.</p></item>
<item><p>In the <gui>Command</gui> group, set <gui>When command exits</gui> to <gui>Close terminal</gui>, <gui>Restart command</gui> or <gui>Hold terminal</gui>.</p></item>
</steps>

  <p>With <gui>Hold terminal</gui>, the terminal shows how the command ended,
  and you can start it again with <gui style="button">Relaunch</gui>, or
  start your shell in its place with <gui style="button">Run Shell</gui>.</p>

  <note style="tip">
    <p>If a <link xref="pref-custom-command">custom command</link> prints
    something and exits at once, use <gui>Hold terminal</gui> so that you can
    read its output.</p>
  </note>

